      "writtenOn": "2026-04-24T19:31:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for taking a look Giuliano and Todd\n\nBased on your mentions I generated a \"master\" abi symbol list that incluces all the symbols from across the different vendor abi lists. I used this to represent the stable KMI and then checked each of the modules we\u0027re converting to GKI modules here against that list, to see whether there are any modules that have all of their (vmlinux) symbols already included in that symbol list (I made sure to ignore any symbols that are provided by other modules).\n\nBased on that approach, I found that out of these 44 modules, 30 of them already have all their symbols included in the master symbol list, meaning they can be built as tegra vendor modules without impacting the KMI. I\u0027ll just add their symbols to the tegra ABI symbol list but they should already be covered by other vendor abi lists.\n\nThere are 14 modules among these that have symbols missing from the KMI. In total, these 14 modules require 96 additional symbols in the KMI.\n\nThe 14 modules are listed below alongside the number of additional symbols they require:\n```\ndrivers/usb/storage/ums-usbat.ko- 16\t\ndrivers/usb/storage/ums-sddr09.ko - 18\t\ndrivers/usb/storage/ums-cypress.ko\tgki - 13\t\nsound/soc/generic/snd-soc-audio-graph-card.ko - 1\t\nsound/pci/hda/snd-hda-codec-hdmi.ko - 1\t\ndrivers/gpu/drm/tiny/simpledrm.ko - 8\t\nfs/pstore/pstore_zone.ko - 2\t\nfs/pstore/pstore_blk.ko - 3\t\ndrivers/net/phy/microchip.ko - 2\t\ndrivers/net/usb/lan78xx.ko\tgki - 4\t\ndrivers/i2c/muxes/i2c-mux-gpio.ko - 4\t\nfs/efivarfs/efivarfs.ko - 20\t\ncrypto/arc4.ko - 2\t\narch/arm64/crypto/aes-neon-blk.ko - 2\n```\n\nWhat do you guys think based on this?",
      "parentUuid": "8640bb88_0a7c4fc5",
      "revId": "490fd0b7a7a69e3647b0d8cb16e1fa97eec4ab79",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
